  "query_preview": "..\nA subtropical ridge extending from the northeast has weakened the \ntrades, bringing light and variable winds to the region. Visible \nsatellite imagery depicted scattered showers over the CNMI all day, \nand island-effect thunderstorms over Guam early this evening. The \nfrictional force between the ridges to the southwest and northeast as\nwell as adequate Precipitable Water (PWAT) values around 2.10 inches\nwill keep scattered showers for the entire region in tonight's \nforecast. As for tomorrow, model guidance shows higher winds and \nincreased moisture for the CNMI compared to Guam, so scattered \nshowers will remain in the forecast, adding isolated thunderstorms \nfor Guam as island convection remains a possibility due to light and \nvariable winds. The dry trade-wind regime may return to the region \nstarting Friday, possibly limiting showers and increasing winds \nthrough the weekend.",
